From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] apklayer: mutex-timedlock

Timed locking must unwrap the same mutex as normal locking. Falling back to glibc passes it a bionic object and overwrites its stored native pointer.

apklayer patch: step 5 of the former scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh (see docs/PATCHES.md), patch 0005 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
index 3247a79..68fa5a3 100644
--- a/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
+++ b/pthread_wrapper/libpthread.c
@@ -509,6 +509,14 @@ int bionic_pthread_mutex_trylock(bionic_mutex_t *mutex)
 	return pthread_mutex_trylock(mutex->glibc);
 }
 
+/* apklayer patch: Android Mutex::timedLock and libc++ timed_mutex. */
+int bionic_pthread_mutex_timedlock(bionic_mutex_t *mutex, const struct timespec *abstime)
+{
+	assert(mutex);
+	INIT_IF_NOT_MAPPED(mutex, default_pthread_mutex_init);
+	return pthread_mutex_timedlock(mutex->glibc, abstime);
+}
+
 int bionic_pthread_mutex_unlock(bionic_mutex_t *mutex)
 {
 	assert(mutex);
